Why Choose Bottomline?
Are you ready to transform the way businesses pay and get paid? Bottomline is a global leader in business payments and cash management, with over 35 years of experience and moving more than $16 trillion in payments annually. We're looking for passionate individuals to join our team and help drive impactful results for our customers. If you're dedicated to delighting customers and promoting growth and innovation - we want you on our team!
Service Delivery - Implementation Consultant&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Department: Service Delivery&nbsp;
Location: Theale (Hybrid)&nbsp;
Reporting To: Implementation Services Delivery Manager&nbsp;
&nbsp;
• Please note that this is an entry level role
• The role is based in Theale, Reading and would require 3 days' attendance per week.
Job Summary&nbsp;
The Implementation Consultant:&nbsp;
&nbsp;
• is responsible for the delivery of technical orders for Bottomline’s payments customers.&nbsp;
• will install, configure and test products on customer environments.&nbsp;
• will develop customer workflows, profiles or mapping templates as needed.&nbsp;
• must routinely deliver project work that conforms to the defined best practices in line with delivery quality models.&nbsp;
• must communicate effectively between both internal channels (project office, account managers, other implementation consultants) and external customers.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Job Responsibilities&nbsp;
&nbsp;
• Installation of payments solutions and configuring applications in Customers’ environments following the standard process (remotely via Microsoft Teams or on-site as required).&nbsp;
• Data file validation.&nbsp;
• Building of Bacs Applications, Cheque profiles and Webforms.&nbsp;
• Migration of existing Direct Debit Management / Cheques to our cloud-based solutions.&nbsp;
• Customer Solution Training.&nbsp;
• Customer Support (Go-live support, UAT support).&nbsp;
• Troubleshooting and fault finding of deployed solutions.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Development tasks will involve the use of in-house scripts, templates and tools, alongside Microsoft Windows and database technologies.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
• Providing advice and consultancy to Project Office staff and customers.&nbsp;
• Testing development packages (including the completion of test evidence and sign-off forms).&nbsp;
• Testing of deployment packages and troubleshooting of issues for pre-live project implementations.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Customers&nbsp;
Delight our customers by:&nbsp;
&nbsp;
• Ensuring that the delivered scope of works is sufficient to complete the work requested by the customer; identifying any ambiguities and presenting these clearly to the project office or directly to the customer.&nbsp;
• Ensuring that scheduled jobs are dealt with promptly to the departmental service levels.&nbsp;
• Ensuring all data file checks are responded to promptly in line with the departmental service levels.&nbsp;
• Providing high quality, consistent output in line with agreed best practice processes.&nbsp;
• Commit to a ‘right first time’ approach.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Teamwork&nbsp;
Work together by:&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
• Supporting the Implementation Consultants and Project Office teams.&nbsp;
• Interpreting and communicating activities in a clear manner.&nbsp;
• Where required, educating and training other team members on specific technical skills.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Innovate&nbsp;
Innovating by:&nbsp;
&nbsp;
• Participating in peer review of tasks, challenging and reviewing best practices.&nbsp;
• Engaging with new project work.&nbsp;
• Developing knowledge of new methods and tools that are applicable to the role and the business.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Improve (KPI’s)&nbsp;
Constantly improving by:&nbsp;
&nbsp;
• Participating in peer review of development deliverables, challenging and reviewing best practices.&nbsp;
• Taking ownership of a particular development skillset as the primary consultant.&nbsp;
• Continuing to challenge personal ability throughout the role.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Initial Technical Requirements&nbsp;
The following initial technical knowledge is required for the role:&nbsp;
&nbsp;
• Windows Server Operating Systems.&nbsp;
• General understanding of project workflow.&nbsp;
• General familiarity of databases.&nbsp;
• General understanding of software development and implementation processes.&nbsp;
• Please note that this is an entry level role
• The role is based in Theale, Reading and would require 3 days' attendance per week.
&nbsp;
Supplementary Technical Requirements&nbsp;&nbsp;
The following software tools will be used during the role so any additional knowledge of these would be beneficial, but not mandatory, as would be developed during the role:&nbsp;
&nbsp;
• Microsoft Teams&nbsp;
• VMWare Workstation.&nbsp;
• Any knowledge of HSMs, certificates and PKI technologies.&nbsp;
• Networking: Any exposure to network concepts and services would be beneficial, e.g. Proxy Servers and Firewalls.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Other Requirements&nbsp;
&nbsp;
• 1 - 3 years’ experience in Service Delivery or Technical Support.&nbsp;
• Ability to communicate at varying levels of technical detail with customers &amp; other colleagues in one-on-one and group situations.&nbsp;
• Capable and comfortable working in a fast-paced environment.&nbsp;
• Capacity for problem solving and decision making.&nbsp;
• Be a team player but able to work on own initiative.&nbsp;
• Have the ability to plan and prioritise their own work.&nbsp;
• A responsible attitude. Professional and positive.&nbsp;
• Well organised.&nbsp;
• Calmness under pressure.&nbsp;
• Open and honest.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
We welcome talent at all career stages and are dedicated to understanding and supporting additional needs. We're proud to be an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating an inclusive and open environment for everyone.

WHO ARE WE
Cognism is the leading provider of European B2B data and sales intelligence. Ambitious businesses of every size use our platform to discover, connect, and engage with qualified decision-makers faster and close more deals. Headquartered in London with global offices, Cognism’s contact data and contextual signals are trusted by thousands of revenue teams to eliminate the guesswork from prospecting.
As Executive Assistant and London office Manager at Cognism, you’ll sit at the operational heart of the business – responsible both for the smooth day-to-day running of our London HQ and for executive support across several members of our Executive Leadership Team.&nbsp;
On the office side, you’ll be responsible for creating a well-organised, efficient and welcoming office environment, supporting teams across the company, and managing the administrative processes that keep the organisation running effectively. On the executive side, you’ll provide diary and correspondence management for the CEO, CFO and CHRO, with lighter-touch support for the CPTO, CISO and CLO on board-related matters. &nbsp;
Office Operations and Environment
• Oversee the day-to-day running of the office, ensuring it is clean, well-stocked and fit for purpose. Manage relationships with building management, suppliers, and service providers. Act as the first point of contact for all facilities-related matters.
• Ensure the office meets all health and safety requirements. Maintain records, conduct risk assessments, and liaise with external parties on building compliance and certifications
• Own procurement of office supplies, office equipment, and amenities, negotiating with vendors to ensure value for money.
• Provision and deprovision London office access passes for employees, and arrange guest bookings for those temporarily visiting
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Executive Diary &amp; Correspondence Management
• Full diary management for CEO, CHRO, CFO
• Provide light diary management and meeting/collaboration preparation support for CPTO, CISO and CLO in relation to board preparation
• Align board agendas across stakeholders; own the annual board cadence across all 11 members/ observers, including ad-hoc sessions
• Coordinate all logistics for in-person and remote board meetings
• Maintain the yearly ELT travel tracker, supporting travel bookings (hotel, flight, train, car) and expense submissions for CEO
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Leadership and Company Operations
• Organise and support deep dives and ELT meetings across the organisation, for both large and small groups
• Collate and distribute Townhall content, owning Townhall day logistics including in-person and Zoom set-up
• Keep Townhall/ ELT/ SLT/ People/ Investor/ Board distribution lists and slack channels up-to-date
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
People, Offsite and Culture Support
• Support onboarding for new joiners, ensuring their workspace is welcoming from day one. Run each new starter through our Fire Evacuation plan.
• Help coordinate company events, offsites and social activities that contribute to a positive office culture. From time to time, you may also assist with coordinating administrative tasks and cultural events for our Cologne, Paris and Boston offices
• Organise ELT/ SLT offsites end-to-end: aligning diaries across all attendees, booking meeting rooms, catering, hotels and dinners where applicable, and tracking dietary requirements. Coordinate agenda logistics directly with the CEO
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
WHY COGNISM
At Cognism, we’re not just building a company - we’re building an inclusive community of brilliant, diverse people who&nbsp;support, challenge, and inspire each other every day. If you’re looking for a place where your work truly&nbsp;makes an impact, you’re in the right spot!
Our values aren’t just words on a page—they guide how we work, how we treat each other, and how we grow together. They shape our culture, drive our success, and ensure that everyone feels valued, heard, and empowered to do their best work.
Here’s what we stand for:
🤝 We Own the Outcome Together.
🤓&nbsp;We Deeply Understand our Customers.&nbsp;
🏆&nbsp;We Celebrate Impact Wherever It Comes From.
At Cognism, we are committed to fostering an inclusive, diverse, and supportive workplace. We welcome applications from individuals typically underrepresented in tech, so if this role excites you but you’re unsure if you meet every requirement, we encourage you to apply!
&nbsp;

D2L is a cloud company that is modernizing education and building the Future of Work. The old models of teaching and learning are in the midst of the largest transformation in history, and D2L is at the heart of that fundamental shift.&nbsp;
New models of teaching and learning enable a personalized, student-centric experience – and deliver&nbsp;improved retention, engagement, satisfaction, and results for learners of all ages – in schools, campuses, and companies.
D2L is disrupting the way the world learns, by providing the next generation learning environment and solutions to engage and inspire learners. And most importantly, by giving customers a platform that is easy, flexible, and smart.&nbsp;No other company provides a solution as robust and innovative as D2L.
D2L has had a singular mission for 25 years and is dedicated to that same mission in the years ahead: to transform the way the world learns – and by doing so, we will help improve human potential globally.
Every application we receive is personally reviewed by a member of our Talent Acquisition team - yes, a real person looks at your resume! While we use AI tools internally to streamline tasks like meeting notes, summaries, and administrative work, these tools never rank resumes, make hiring decisions, or influence candidate evaluations.
General Description:&nbsp;
Our ideal candidate is an experienced strategic people and business leader responsible for building a predictable, high-performing business development engine across APAC and EMEA. This role translates company and revenue priorities into regional operating plans, develops managers and BDR talent, and partners across Sales, Marketing, RevOps, Enablement and Finance to create qualified pipeline and measurable commercial impact.&nbsp;
The Manager of Business Development will manage and grow a team of Business Development Representatives in APAC and EMEA and responsible for driving qualifying opportunities that build pipeline for the Named and Strategic sales organization. This individual will be a coach who has a deep understanding how to overcome common obstacles and has a passion to teach other how to become a top performer.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Success is measured by team activity, quality, conversion, predictability and scalability of the pipeline engine, the strength of the talent bench, and the leader’s ability to influence outcomes beyond their immediate team.
Major Responsibilities:&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Own the regional operating strategy: Build and execute an APAC and EMEA BDR plan aligned to segment, territory, pipeline and revenue priorities; establish clear goals, capacity assumptions, coverage models and quarterly execution rhythms.&nbsp;
• Deliver business outcomes: Hold the organization accountable for qualified pipeline, stage progression, conversion, forecast accuracy and quality. Identify risks early and lead corrective action.&nbsp;
• Lead through influence: Partner with Sales leadership, Marketing, RevOps, Enablement, Finance and Product to improve routing, campaign-to-pipeline conversion, account prioritization, messaging, process and inspection.&nbsp;
• Build a scalable system: Define and improve the operating model, reporting, dashboards, cadences, qualification standards, handoffs and governance required to make performance repeatable across markets.&nbsp;
• Represent the region: Bring clear insights, recommendations and trade-offs to senior leadership, using data and frontline evidence to shape broader business decisions.&nbsp;
Performance and Operational Leadership&nbsp;
• Create a predictable regional performance-management rhythm spanning weekly inspection, monthly business reviews and quarterly planning.&nbsp;
• Define leading and lagging indicators, including activity quality, connect and meeting conversion, meeting-to-S1/S2 progression, pipeline contribution, coverage, attainment and forecast confidence.&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Use Salesforce, Salesloft, 6sense, ChatGPT, Power BI and other systems to diagnose performance, improve visibility and ensure data integrity.&nbsp;
• Turn trends and performance gaps into practical experiments, documented actions and measurable improvement plans.&nbsp;
• Maintain disciplined operating standards while adapting execution to APAC and EMEA market realities, segments and cultures.&nbsp;
People Leadership and Performance&nbsp;
• Lead, coach and develop BDRs and managers through clear expectations, high-quality 1:1s, call coaching, deal/pipeline reviews and individualized development plans.&nbsp;
• Build a strong talent pipeline and succession plan; make thoughtful hiring, onboarding, performance and promotion decisions.&nbsp;
• Create an inclusive, accountable and high-performing culture where people understand the connection between their work, customer value and D2L’s mission&nbsp;
• Develop future sellers by delegating meaningful ownership, creating stretch opportunities and sharing practical expertise across the broader BD organization.&nbsp;
• Address performance issues directly and fairly, balancing empathy with clarity, consistency and business accountability.&nbsp;
Cross Functional Leadership&nbsp;
• Partner with regional and segment Sales leaders to define target-account priorities, engagement plans, qualification standards and handoff expectations.&nbsp;
• Work with Marketing to improve campaign strategy, event follow-up, lead quality, nurture paths and contribution to pipeline.&nbsp;
• Collaborate with RevOps and Enablement on process design, reporting, tooling adoption, training and continuous improvement.&nbsp;
• Build trust across functions and resolve competing priorities through clear communication, sound judgment and shared outcomes.&nbsp;
• Share market, customer and competitive insight that improves messaging, plays and go-to-market decisions&nbsp;
D2L Leadership Competencies&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Leads by Example with personal and professional integrity, high accountability and say/do ratio&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Boundaryless collaboration and influence skills both within team, peer group and broader organization. Effective communicator with a proven track record of success.&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Delivers Awesome Outcomes: Strategic mindset and business acumen, with strong prioritization skills and a focus on organizational outcomes vs. team tasks. Effective problem solver, able to achieve results individually and through others, in fast paced, deadline-driven environments.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Talent Magnet: Talent-focused leader, with demonstrated ability to coach, build and lead a high performing, diverse team.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Better, Smarter, Faster: An agile learner, with a growth mindset, attention to detail and organizational skills. An operationally minded leader, with a focus on continuous improvement and innovation.&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Wins Hearts and Minds: An effective communicator, with the ability to connect the why and the what. A change agent, with proven delegation, motivation, and team building skills.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
Suggested Qualifications/Experience:&nbsp;
• 3+ Years of experience leading high-performing sales development team &nbsp;
• 2+ years of experience selling software and SaaS &nbsp;
• Experience with Salesforce, Salesloft, AI and other sales engagement tools.  &nbsp;
• Have experience leading remote teams&nbsp;
• Have experience with outbound /cold prospecting and working with inbound leads  &nbsp;
• Lead by example and a willingness to get into the trenches with the front line  &nbsp;
• Excellent written/oral communications and analytical skills  &nbsp;
• Excellent interpersonal skills, able to interface effectively across levels and functions  &nbsp;
• Experience training, mentoring, and growing an outbound process.&nbsp;
Don’t meet every single requirement?&nbsp;We strongly encourage you to still apply! At D2L, we are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive environment. We encourage your application even if you don't believe you meet every single qualification outlined, because we love to help our people grow and develop!
Why we're awesome:
&nbsp;
At D2L, we are dedicated to providing you with the tools to do the best work of your life. While some of our perks and benefits may vary depending on location or employment type, we are proud to provide employees with the following through&nbsp;#LifeAtD2L:
• Impactful work transforming the way the world learns
• Flexible work arrangements
• Learning and Growth opportunities
• Tuition reimbursement of up to $4,000 CAD for continuing education through our SkillsWave Program
• 2 Paid Days off for SkillsWave-related activities like exams or final assignments
• Employee wellbeing (Access to mental health services, EFAP program, financial planning and more)
• Retirement planning
• 2 Paid Volunteer Days
• Competitive Benefits Package
• Home Internet Reimbursements
• Employee Referral Program
• Wellness Reimbursement
• Employee Recognition
• Social Events
• Dog Friendly Offices Spaces at our HQ in Kitchener, Winnipeg, Vancouver and Melbourne offices.

