Marketing Lead Location:&nbsp;&nbsp;Hybrid (home-based &amp; working with Kerv Digital office/customer site visits as required) Office locations – Longbridge, London &amp; Nottingham
ABOUT KERV&nbsp;
At Kerv we harness the power of technology for the good of our people, our customers, our society and our planet. Technology is the enabler; impact is how we judge success.&nbsp;
As a certified B Corp and Great Place To Work, we care deeply about how we show up for our people, our customers and the world around us. These aren’t badges for us, they reflect how we work every day and the standards we hold ourselves to.&nbsp;
With more than 900 specialists and over 1,600 technical certifications, we are bringing together expertise across cloud, AI, compliance, data, customer experience and business applications. Working as one connected team, we solve complex challenges and stay accountable from strategy through to delivery, adoption and ongoing improvement.&nbsp;
We help organisations build secure, well governed foundations, leverage more from their technology and unlock new opportunities through innovation and AI. Our focus is on making technology work in the real world and delivering lasting value.&nbsp;
THE ROLE&nbsp;
You’ll be part of the Marketing Team in Kerv Digital.&nbsp;
At Kerv Digital, we help organisations unlock the power of technology to transform how they work, engage customers and drive business value. We combine deep expertise across Microsoft Business Applications, Power Platform, AI, DevOps, Data and cloud technologies. With a strong focus on outcomes and real-world value, we make digital transformation feel tangible, purposeful and fast-moving.&nbsp;
We are actively seeking a Marketing Lead for the Private Sector to work closely with the Marketing Director and senior management to research, plan, execute and report on marketing strategies that are measurable and aligned to our sector sales strategy. We’re looking for an individual who has proven experience in managing campaigns and is keen for the next step in their career to be responsible for marketing across multiple industries. The successful candidate will work across our Private Sector sub-verticals: Commercial, Housing, Social Enterprise, Charities and Further Education. You will develop campaigns that reflect the needs of each audience, building tailored awareness of our brand and finding customers ready to engage with sales.&nbsp;&nbsp;
As an experienced technology marketeer, you will know how to put the right content in front of the right people to generate interest and sales opportunities and generate pipeline. You will bring a mix of content, account-based marketing (ABM), partner marketing, events and digital campaign experience. Working in a busy, growth-focused marketing department, you will balance hands-on delivery with campaign planning and commercial reporting. A strong understanding of our core sectors and ideal customer profiles (ICPs) will be critical to identifying target accounts, creating relevant messaging and working with sales to turn engagement into measurable pipeline. You will also work with Microsoft and our wider partners to identify joint marketing opportunities and align campaigns with relevant sector and technology priorities.&nbsp;&nbsp;
We’re willing to invest in an individual looking to make the next step in their career and support with training and growth plans to make a stamp on the way marketing is done within our organisation. If you are looking to work within an existing, talented team by getting your hands dirty with content and campaigns one day, then talking strategy and reports directly with Senior Management the next, this is the role for you.&nbsp; You’ll be used to working across multiple departments and have fun doing it as part of a global team. By helping us tell our story you will help us show clients what it is like to work with Kerv and inspire potential recruits to join us. You’ll be rewarded with a clear career trajectory and training opportunities, as well as the opportunity to learn more about cutting edge tech.&nbsp;
You will be given freedom to help develop our Private Sector marketing strategy, tailoring activity to each sub-vertical, and work with the wider team to understand and implement the Kerv brand values and make sure our USP shines through. You will work closely with our technical teams to translate expertise in Microsoft Dynamics 365, Power Platform, Azure, data and AI into relevant, outcome-led campaigns. You will actively look for opportunities to use AI to improve marketing insight, campaign delivery and efficiency, as well as identify customer needs that could inform campaigns for our AI capabilities.&nbsp;
Responsibilities:  Candidates will need to demonstrate experience or an aptitude for:&nbsp;
• Close collaboration with sales to agree target accounts, deliver account-based marketing campaigns and share accountability for generating and progressing pipeline.&nbsp;
• Developing a strong understanding of our core Private Sector sub-verticals, their buying needs and ideal customer profiles, using this insight to prioritise accounts and tailor events and campaigns.&nbsp;
• Budgeting and ROI forecasting for campaigns.&nbsp;
• Planning and prioritising marketing activity, managing stakeholder requests and coordinating elements of event delivery, including timelines, logistics, promotion and follow-up, alongside wider campaign commitments.&nbsp;
• Working with Microsoft, other partners and suppliers to develop joint campaigns, identify relevant opportunities and grow our reach across the Private Sector sub-verticals.&nbsp;
• Pitching and running with GTM and ABM campaigns and approaches to senior management with budget control and management&nbsp;
• Using Microsoft Dynamics CRM and its marketing tools to manage campaign activity, maintain accurate account and contact data, track engagement and connect marketing activity to sales opportunities.&nbsp;
• Working closely with our internal design team, comfortable with the Adobe suite, and an eye for design&nbsp;
• Maintaining and improving upon Kerv Digital’s social media presence&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Marketing Reporting and Metrics: Report on campaign and content performance, target-account engagement, qualified leads, marketing-sourced and influenced pipeline, and ROI, using Dynamics CRM to demonstrate contribution to growth.&nbsp;
• Identifying and testing practical AI opportunities to improve research, targeting, content and campaign efficiency, with appropriate checks for accuracy, brand consistency and data privacy.&nbsp;
&nbsp;Required skills / experience: &nbsp;
• An experienced marketing professional with around 5+ years’ experience in B2B technology marketing&nbsp;&nbsp;
• A proactive, commercially minded approach, with strong organisational skills essential to working in a busy, growth-focused marketing department. You will need to balance and prioritise competing workloads, manage incoming demand and agree realistic deadlines with stakeholders across campaigns and event activity.&nbsp;
• Strong sector research and audience insight skills, with the ability to define ideal customer profiles and translate these into targeted account-based marketing campaigns in partnership with sales.&nbsp;
• Experience of using CRM and marketing platforms to measure campaign effectiveness and demonstrate pipeline contribution. Familiarity with Microsoft Dynamics CRM and its marketing tools would be an advantage.&nbsp;
• An interest in AI and a practical approach to identifying opportunities to improve marketing performance and communicate relevant customer outcomes.&nbsp;
• Previous experience of working with Microsoft or within its partner ecosystem, including joint marketing activity, would be a bonus but is not essential.&nbsp;
We’re also looking for people that fit how we work, which is something like; &nbsp;
• A determined individual who is willing to work hard to build a successful marketing career&nbsp;
• A natural interest in technology would be a huge advantage&nbsp;
• A people person who can work with various stakeholders&nbsp;
• Happy to work as part of the wider team in both Kerv Digital India and UK, offering honest feedback to senior management&nbsp;
• Excellent spoken and written communication&nbsp;
• Ability to work to tight targets and timescales&nbsp;
&nbsp;
What we can do for you: We’re a transparent, honest and fiercely equal employer that believes completely in providing the best possible work experience for our employee’s: &nbsp;
Real Flexibility&nbsp;– A healthy approach for most of our teams seems to be splitting three ways between home, customer sites and the office.&nbsp;
Awesome Environment&nbsp;– all of our employee’s will tell you that we foster an easy going environment, are experts at what we do and care deeply about what we work on – the company was started specifically to find a way for people to take more enjoyment from their work.&nbsp;
Interesting Work&nbsp;– these days most of our customers are household names and many of our projects have an important impact on the world around us. The kind of things we do regularly include working with not-for-profits to transform how they leverage technology, working with public bodies to shape digital services and working with top tier private entities to bring genuinely new and meaningful products and services to market.&nbsp;
Great Benefits&nbsp;– all the usual suspects and then some. Some highlights include excellent professional development support including frequent in-house training for tech. you can’t get trained on anywhere else, private healthcare, company pension and, well stocked cupboards with tasty goodies (we’re a food first company too).
Recognition &amp; Growth&nbsp;– Recognized as a 'Great Place to Work' in both the UK and India, our commitment to excellence goes beyond our products and services. Our culture is a testament to the dedicated technologists who work tirelessly to drive our vision forward. Being a part of means embracing a culture of innovation, collaboration, and mutual respect. Our teams thrive in an atmosphere that promotes continuous learning and growth.
&nbsp;
OUR VALUES&nbsp;
At Kerv, we’re building something special and building it to last. Our values shape how we work, how we treat each other and how we deliver for our customers:&nbsp;
• Think Customer First – we put our customers at the heart of every decision&nbsp;
• Team is Everything – we collaborate, support each other, and win together&nbsp;
• Spread Good Vibes – we bring positivity, energy and respect into everything we do&nbsp;
• Build Future – we look ahead, innovate and create lasting impact&nbsp;
• Do the Right Thing – we act with integrity and always do what’s fair and honest&nbsp;
&nbsp;
We’re looking for people who bring these values to life in how they work every day. We want everybody to feel valued, included and love working together. With an uncompromising pursuit of amazing employee experience, we always strive to do the right thing. We believe and will relentlessly promote and support the power of diversity, equality and belonging, through collaboration and creating exceptional solutions together.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Equal opportunity statement
We welcome applications from all qualified individuals regardless of age, disability, gender identity, marital or civil partnership status, pregnancy or maternity, race, religion or belief, gender, sexual orientation or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. &nbsp;
Kerv encourages applications from people of all backgrounds, experiences and perspectives. Our recruitment decisions are based solely on skills, experience, qualifications and business needs, and we provide reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process where required.&nbsp;
You will live the Kerv values…
• Think Customer First
• Team is everything
• Spread good vibes
• Build future
• Do the right thing
At Kerv, we’re building something special and we’re building it to last. We want everybody to feel valued, included and love working together. With an uncompromising pursuit of amazing employee experience, we always strive to do the right thing. We believe and will relentlessly promote and support the power of diversity, equality and belonging, through collaboration and creating exceptional solutions together.

Langan provides expert Civil, Geotechnical, Traffic and Geo-Environmental engineering consulting services for major developers, renewable energy producers, energy companies, corporations, healthcare systems, colleges/universities, and large infrastructure programs around the world. Our employees collaborate seamlessly and gain valuable hands-on experience that fosters career growth. Langan culture is entrepreneurial from advancing innovative technical solutions, to participating in robust training and knowledge sharing, to making progressive change within the communities we live and work.
&nbsp;
Consistently ranked among the top ten “Best Firms to Work For” and Engineering News-Record’s top 50 firms worldwide, Langan attracts and retains the best talent in the industry. Employees thrive at Langan, a firm that fosters an inclusive and supportive work environment for all; prioritizes wellbeing, health, and safety; encourages volunteerism and philanthropy; offers workplace flexibility, along with carbon-neutral office spaces; and empowers individuals to contribute their skills and knowledge to make impactful contributions.
&nbsp;
Job Summary
Langan International, UK, Ltd. is seeking an&nbsp;Associate Engineer&nbsp;to join its collaborative team in&nbsp;London.&nbsp;This hands-on individual will serve a key function developing new clients for the firm as well as designing land development engineering projects for a wide variety of exciting projects in the area. In this role, you will have the opportunity to manage and mentor a team of multidisciplinary engineers, lead design efforts, and develop and maintain clients for the firm.&nbsp;
Job Responsibilities
• Work closely with office leadership to develop growth plans and ensure staff utilization;&nbsp;
• Possess an entrepreneurial demeanor and participate in Business Development activities by developing new clients for the firm and maintaining relationships with existing clients;&nbsp;
• Design and oversee design on a variety of projects including layout, grading, drainage, infrastructure, erosion and sediment control, etc. from concept through completion;
• Lead all aspects of land development engineering including the integration of geotechnical and geoenvironmental engineering;
• Provide leadership, mentorship and coaching to a team of technical staff.&nbsp;Responsible for performance management, professional growth and career development of civil personnel; and
• Performs other duties as requested.
Qualifications
• Bachelor's degree in Civil Engineering, Master's degree a plus;
• 8+ years experience in related civil land development engineering;&nbsp;
• Proven leadership and ability to function as a seller/doers;
• Knowledge of local land use entitlement processes and regulations;
• Demonstrated expertise in all aspects of land development engineering including the integration of geotechnical and environmental engineering;
• Expertise in stormwater management design, LID and hydrologic/hydraulic analysis and design;
• Experience in technical and proposal writing;
• Strong client development and client management abilities;
• Proficiency of AutoCAD or Civil 3D (preferred);
• Active participation in professional organizations;
• Ability to effectively work independently and in a team environment, and to mentor staff engineers;
• Excellent written and verbal communication skills;
• Strong attention to detail with excellent analytical, multitasking, and judgment capabilities; and&nbsp;
• Possess reliable transportation for client meetings and job site visits and a valid driver’s license in good standing.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Langan provides a rich array of programs and benefits to help its employees advance their careers and enhance the quality of their lives. Our comprehensive compensation package includes: full-time employment company paid private medical insurance; group income protection; group life insurance; paid time off including maternity and parental leave; UK Workplace pension with company contribution; employee referral and professional license bonuses; and educational reimbursement.
&nbsp;
Langan offers employee resource groups; flexible work schedules; extensive training; wellness programs; buddy and mentoring programs; and much more!
&nbsp;
Langan is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all qualified applicants and employees. We believe that an inclusive workplace is essential for the well-being and success of our employees.
&nbsp;
Please review our Applicant Privacy Notice at Collection to understand how we collect, use, and retain your personal information: &nbsp;https://www.langan.com/langan-notice-at-collection
&nbsp;
&nbsp;

Movable Ink scales content personalization for marketers through data-activated content generation and AI decisioning. The world’s most innovative brands rely on Movable Ink to maximize revenue, simplify workflow and boost marketing agility. Headquartered in New York City with close to 600 employees, Movable Ink serves its global client base with operations throughout North America, Central America, Europe, Australia, and Japan.
--
Movable Ink is seeking a Marketing Coordinator, International to join our dynamic team. This role will play a key role in executing marketing efforts across all regions outside the US, including EMEA and ANZ. Reporting to the Associate Director, International marketing,&nbsp; this generalist role provides multi-channel support across a variety of marketing disciplines with a key focus on regional events, gifting programs, and campaign management.&nbsp; This role also will play a strong role in supporting the global marketing organization. This role is an excellent opportunity for an ambitious, fast-paced marketer looking to build a comprehensive foundation in B2B demand generation and understand where their future long-term career path lies.
&nbsp;
Responsibilities:
• Support with the execution of our International event plan, including hosted events, partner events and third party events.&nbsp;
• Support regional and global gifting campaigns, swag warehouse logistics, and platform deployment to support sales and business development outreach
• Support global campaign management initiatives, including project management of global campaigns as well as local ABM-efforts.&nbsp;
Qualifications:
• 2+ years of marketing experience, preferably in a B2B capacity and/or events capacity&nbsp;
• Strong attention to detail and ability to work in a fast-paced environment&nbsp;
• Ability to project manage and multi-task effectively&nbsp;
• Creative and thinks outside the box
• Working independently as needed&nbsp;
• Strong communication skills and experience working cross-functionally.
• Preferred but not required: Experience with marketing and sales tools like Canva, Bizabo, Salesforce, Sendoso, etc.&nbsp;
The base pay range for this position is £34-£44/year, which can include additional bonus depending on the position ultimately offered, in addition to a full range of medical, financial, and/or other benefits. The base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.
Studies have shown that women, communities of color, and historically underrepresented people are less likely to apply to jobs unless they meet every single qualification. We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive culture where all Inkers can thrive. If you’re excited about the role but don’t meet all of the abovementioned qualifications, we encourage you to apply. Our differences bring a breadth of knowledge and perspectives that makes us collectively stronger.
We welcome and employ people regardless of race, color, gender identity or expression, religion, genetic information, parental or pregnancy status, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, ethnicity, family or marital status, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, disability, Veteran status, or other protected characteristics. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer.

The role will be working within a mature 2nd line support team, with responsibility for resolving incidents raised by customers, via the NEC Service Desk, for the CONNECT Police software. You will be joining a team with strong technical background who formerly had roles in development, end user support and software implementation disciplines. About the role: ● Provide software application support;
● Own and undertake the investigation of complex application incidents;
● Recreate scenarios on internal test environments to provide evidence of defects;
● Identify and document workarounds;
● Work within contractual SLAs;
● Work to ITIL aligned support process procedures;
● Work closely with other NEC Teams and 3rd parties;
● Participate in an Out of Hours on call rota.
KNOWLEDGE, QUALIFICATIONS & EXPERIENCE
• Experience of working with complex bespoke software applications either in a Support, Development or QA role;
• Experience of working within a structured process driven environment;
• Experience of using an IT Service Management tool or similar;
• ITIL Foundation certificate;
• Experience of investigating data related issues within a relational database;
• Capability to generate and manipulate SQL scripts used to query and manage database content;
• Ability to check log files and restart services on a number of operating systems including Microsoft Windows and UNIX Solaris;
• Understand principles of software development within an ISO 9001/ISO 20000 accredited environment
Exposure to the following:
• Microsoft Windows Servers environments;
• UNIX Solaris servers environments;
• Java;
• Ensemble;
• Microsoft .net;
• SQL;
• Oracle;
• jetnexus;
• Javascript;
• HTML;
• Active MQ
PERSONAL SKILLS AND COMPETENCES
• Self-motivated and persistent with a desire to learn and enjoys helping people;
• Demonstrate solid analytical and lateral thinking skills;
• Capable of communicating to technical and non technical staff unambiguously at all levels with respect to support calls;
• Willing to challenge and improve existing processes and practices;
• Proactive and forward thinking to stop incidents occurring;
• Capability to multi-task and balance complex customer and internal priorities;
• Excellent oral and written communication skills;
• Willing to travel (when required) to customer sites;
• Ability to contribute and participate in identification of permanent fixes;
• Exhibit empathy and patience during interactions with customers
We pride ourselves in offering an excellent benefits package, including an above average pension scheme. When you join the team at NEC Software Solutions, you are provided with the following:
