About the Role
You’ll support our Legal Team across LATAM and other international jurisdictions, focusing on betting and gaming regulations, contracts and general legal matters. Your responsibilities will include reviewing and drafting contracts and legal documents, conducting legal research, supporting litigation matters, handling corporate housekeeping and maintaining the legal library, all under the supervision of the Legal Counsel. The role will also provide exposure to broader international legal matters, including commercial contracts, corporate governance and regulatory topics, as well as opportunities to assist with regulatory and certification processes, such as audits, submissions and communications with testing laboratories and regulators, depending on business needs.
What you'll do:
• Review, draft and negotiate commercial agreements (vendor, service, marketing, sponsorship, affiliate, NDAs, data processing), flagging risks and proposing mitigations to the Legal Counsel
• Review corporate, regulatory and commercial documents (policies, terms and conditions, powers of attorney, board resolutions, filings) for accuracy and consistency
• Keep the legal library and contract repository up to date, with version control, templates, standard clauses, a central register of contracts and key dates (renewals, expiries, notice periods), and an internal knowledge base
• Support litigation and administrative proceedings by gathering documents and evidence, tracking deadlines, coordinating with external counsel, and preparing case summaries and status reports
• Carry out legal and regulatory research (contracts, consumer, data protection, corporate, betting/gaming law) and draft junior-level memos and opinions
• Help with corporate housekeeping: entity records, corporate acts, registrations and filings
• Support regulatory and certification processes when needed: tracking certificate and report expiry dates, preparing documents for audits and regulator submissions, and liaising with testing labs;
• Assist the Compliance teams (Brazil, Mexico and other markets.) with policy drafts, regulatory checks and internal processes;
• Handle internal legal requests from business teams (Product, Marketing, Finance, HR), sorting and routing them under the Legal Counsel’s supervision;
• Prepare reports and status updates for leadership and stakeholders;
• Support certification and compliance projects end-to-end: scheduling, tracking progress, coordinating with testing labs (ATFs), preparing documentation for audits and regulator submissions;
• Interface with external certification bodies, testing labs, third-party vendors, and regulators;
• Prepare reports, dashboards and status updates for leadership &amp; stakeholders
What you'll bring:
• Complete Law bachelor's degree and active BAR membership;
• Fluent English and Spanish (written &amp; spoken) are mandatory.&nbsp;
• Attention to detail, strong organizational skills, ability to manage multiple certification tracks
• Analytical mindset, capacity to learn technical standards (software, testing, gaming)
• Proactive, good communicator, ability to liaise across teams and external entities
Even better if:
• Understanding of games, betting, sports and igaming industry.
• Media contract management
• Interest in sports.
• Experience or coursework in contracts and regulatory law, litigation support or in-house legal routines (including internships).
• Availability to work on hybrid model and/or to relocate to São Paulo, Brazil, but fully remote applications will also be considered;

As an ADHD Assessor, you will play a key role in delivering neurodevelopmental assessments for individuals referred to us at The Owl. You will work closely with a multidisciplinary team to provide person-centred assessments - both remotely and in person within your local area (Durham) - and support positive outcomes for clients and families. You will conduct ADHD assessments, developmental case history interviews with patients and families to achieve outcomes in line with clinical guidelines, ensuring reports and recommendations are clear, evidence-based, and completed to a high standard. You will contribute to maintaining excellent clinical standards while supporting the continued growth and reputation of the service.
Please note: this is a permanent, full-time (37.5 hours per week) employed position and we're not looking for contractors at the moment.
Location: Durham (We ask that you have access to your own transport and are happy to travel for up to one hour from your home address)
&nbsp;
What you'll be doing:
• Conduct&nbsp;comprehensive and detailed developmental case history interviews with&nbsp;clients&nbsp;and/or relatives and where relevant,&nbsp;schools&nbsp;or other informants using&nbsp;tool like ACE and DIVA 5&nbsp;to&nbsp;support&nbsp;ADHD assessments&nbsp;to&nbsp;reach&nbsp;an evidence-based understanding that inform diagnosis.&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Liaise with&nbsp;the&nbsp;Multi-Disciplinary&nbsp;Team (MDT)&nbsp;to formulate and reach an understanding of an ADHD assessment to provide evidence-based outcomes&nbsp;using shared formulations&nbsp;and&nbsp;incorporated perspectives to&nbsp;provide a formal diagnosis.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
• Independently manage your own caseload, understand your work in&nbsp;progress&nbsp;and manage KPIs&nbsp;by task&nbsp;prioritisation,&nbsp;escalating&nbsp;risks or delays promptly to ensure&nbsp;timely&nbsp;assessments and meeting service performance. &nbsp;
• Uphold&nbsp;excellent client and staff experiences through maintaining high-quality and thorough assessment services, providing clear communication&nbsp;to foster trust,&nbsp;inclusion&nbsp;and continuous improvement. &nbsp;
• Engage in clinical supervision, 121 and performance review cycles&nbsp;to have access to professional and emotional support when/if required&nbsp;by attending regular&nbsp;sessions, discussing concerns to&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;safe practice&nbsp;and enhance clinical effectiveness.&nbsp;
• Complete required&nbsp;administrative responsibilities which include case note record keeping, incident updating, report completion and risk assessment&nbsp;by documenting clearly following guidelines&nbsp;to ensure&nbsp;accurate&nbsp;records&nbsp;that support continuity of care,&nbsp;safety&nbsp;and compliance. &nbsp;
• Maintain&nbsp;adherence to clinical standard operation procedures&nbsp;by following current pathways and requirements&nbsp;to support service delivery. &nbsp;
• Engage in regular professional development offerings, including CPD sessions, forums and training sessions&nbsp;offered to further career growth and keep up to date with compliance standards&nbsp;to keep skills current and uphold regulatory and service standards.&nbsp;&nbsp;
We'd love it if you're someone who:
• Is able to manage multiple tasks and prioritise effectively.&nbsp;
• Is an excellent communicator and has experience of communicating well through a variety of platforms; (phone, email, virtually) adapting communicative style when needed. &nbsp;
• Can build&nbsp;and sustain great relationships and has experience of doing this both internally and externally.&nbsp;
• Has passion for providing the best possible service to children and their families.&nbsp;
We'd love it if you're someone who has:
• 12 months experience&nbsp;in independently diagnosing ADHD in adults and young people,&nbsp;using&nbsp;diagnostic tools such as DIVA.&nbsp;
• Clinical qualification and registration&nbsp;(in&nbsp;Occupational Therapy,&nbsp;Speech&nbsp;and&nbsp;Language Therapy, Psychology (Clinical, Counselling or Forensic), Mental Health/ Learning,&nbsp;Disability Nursing,&nbsp;Paediatrician).&nbsp;
• Completing&nbsp;the delivery of&nbsp;assessments both in-person&nbsp;and&nbsp;virtually.&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
What you'll get:
• Being part a purpose led organisation, with strong values at the heart of everything we do.
• Working alongside our exceptional clinical leadership team and colleagues.
• The opportunity to do amazing work with our charity 'Waiting Well'
• 50% off assessments, making Autism &amp; ADHD assessments more accessible for you and your family.
• Great leave benefits package includes 25 days of annual leave, increasing by 1 day after only 1 year service up to a maximum of 30 days, your birthday off, and a 'you do you' day to spend on yourself.
• Hybrid &amp; Home working offering the perfect blend of flexibility and in-person collaboration!
• Growth opportunities, as we grow our teams.
• Protected time to connect with colleagues.
• Salary exchange pension - 3% employee, 6% employer contribution
&nbsp;
You’re someone who connects with our values:
• We are one team
• We are reliable
• We are creative
• We are passionate
Don’t be put off if you cannot tick all the boxes. We know that candidates can be put off applying if you don’t feel you are a 100% there, but we would still love to hear from you! We get that a diverse workforce makes a great workforce, this is the reason we are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive culture where our people can turn up, be themselves &amp; thrive.
We want you to be as relaxed as possible during our selection journey which may require an adjustment to our process. We encourage you to be open about what you need so we can adapt and allow you to thrive.
&nbsp;
We may close this vacancy earlier than intended if we receive a high volume of suitable applications. To avoid disappointment, we encourage you to submit your application as soon as possible.
&nbsp;
A note on AI usage
We recognise that using Artificial intelligence (AI) tools in applications is becoming increasingly common. We welcome anything that creates a more inclusive recruitment process and supports candidates from all backgrounds to thrive.&nbsp;
If you do choose to use AI, we gently ask that you ensure all the skills, qualifications, and employment history you list are an accurate reflection of you and your background. The application stage is our first impression of you, so we really want to see your personality and voice shine through!&nbsp;
