**Neurodevelopmental Team Lead (ADHD) - 12 Month FTC**
As the Neurodevelopmental Team Lead, you will lead and support a team of Neurodevelopmental Clinicians, helping them deliver high-quality, clinically sound assessments. You will provide clinical supervision, coaching, workload support and performance management, while promoting professional development and a collaborative team culture. You will monitor service quality and pathway performance, supporting clinicians to meet service expectations and clinical standard whilst working with the Head of Service (ADHD) and other stakeholders to improve clinical pathways, governance and service delivery. Alongside your leadership responsibilities, you will maintain a manageable ADHD assessment caseload, expected to account for approximately 50% of your workload. &nbsp;
Please note: This role is remote but will require some occasional travel to our Pontypool office.
What Will I Be Doing?
• Support Neurodevelopmental Clinicians through regular guidance, feedback and communication so colleagues feel supported, engaged and able to meet service expectations.&nbsp;
• Support development and clinical decision-making through regular individual and group supervision, mentorship, complex case advice and training to build skills and maintain evidence-based clinical standards.&nbsp;
• Coordinate workloads and caseloads by balancing capacity with demand, monitoring pathway flow and resolving barriers to support sustainable workloads, timely assessments and delivery KPIs.&nbsp;
• Support colleagues with clinical and operational challenges by acting as the first escalation point and offering practical guidance so complex queries are addressed promptly.&nbsp;
• Support performance and attendance through regular reviews, constructive feedback and development goals in line with organisational policies to help colleagues meet expectations.&nbsp;
• Contribute to service delivery by conducting ADHD assessments within a manageable caseload, accounting for approximately 50% of your workload, to support access to assessments.&nbsp;
• Support clinical quality by monitoring performance, assessment timelines, reporting and service delivery, and contributing to audits and action plans to maintain organisational standards and improve effectiveness and client outcomes.&nbsp;
• Improve services alongside the Clinical Service Manager and relevant health, education and social care stakeholders by identifying priorities, updating procedures and introducing clinical models, tools and interventions to strengthen integration, consistency, patient care and assessment processes.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
You're Someone Who Is:
• A supportive people leader, coach and mentor who helps a team develop and work effectively.  &nbsp;
• A clear communicator who provides constructive feedback, handles concerns respectfully and helps resolve issues.  &nbsp;
• Able to balance workload distribution, service capacity and expectations in a clinical setting.  &nbsp;
• Analytical and able to review team performance, identify trends and contribute to practical service improvements.  &nbsp;
• Professional and accountable, with a commitment to clinical quality and service excellence.  &nbsp;
• Flexible and able to use initiative as service demands change in a fast-paced, developing environment.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
You're Someone Who Has:
• A professional qualification in psychology, speech and language therapy, occupational therapy, nursing or another relevant field.  &nbsp;
• Additional training in ADHD diagnostic assessments, such as DIVA-5 or ACE.  &nbsp;
• Registration with an appropriate professional body, such as HCPC, RCSLT, NMC, BPS or an equivalent body.  &nbsp;
• Significant experience in ADHD neurodevelopmental assessments and clinical practice.  &nbsp;
• A sound understanding of NICE guidelines, best practice and clinical governance in neurodevelopmental services. 
&nbsp;
You're Someone Who Connects With Our Values:
• We are one team&nbsp;
• We are reliable&nbsp;
• We are creative&nbsp;&nbsp;
• We are passionate&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
What you'll get:
• Being part a purpose led organisation, with strong values at the heart of everything we do.
• Working alongside our exceptional clinical leadership team and colleagues.
• The opportunity to do amazing work with our charity 'Waiting Well'
• 50% off assessments, making Autism &amp; ADHD assessments more accessible for you and your family.
• Great leave benefits package includes 25 days of annual leave, increasing by 1 day after only 1 year service up to a maximum of 30 days, your birthday off, and a 'you do you' day to spend on yourself.
• Hybrid &amp; Home working offering the perfect blend of flexibility and in-person collaboration!
• Growth opportunities, as we grow our teams.
• Protected time to connect with colleagues.
• Salary exchange pension - 3% employee, 6% employer contribution.
&nbsp;
